Description: In-graph speaker protection for Apple Silicon Macs (speakerguardd 1.0)
 speakerguardd 1.0 protects the speakers the way macOS does: the protection
 unit runs inside the PipeWire speaker graph as an LV2 plugin, with the
 amplifiers' voltage and current sense as its second input where the Mac has
 it, driven by that Mac's own tuning bundle.
 .
 It installs beside speakersafetyd and speakerguardd 0.1. Installing it changes
 nothing by itself: at every boot the fleet gate starts exactly one stack, and
 v2 only on a Mac that aurora-speaker-upgrade has switched and whose own tuning
 passed the self-check. Any failure fails closed: the supervisor does not
 start and the kernel keeps the speakers at their safe level.
